          "body": "Munster are hopeful Brian Gleeson will be included in Andy Farrell's Ireland squad, which is due to be named on Wednesday. The 22-year-old number eight has been in Farrell's camp before, and the doubts over Jack Conan's shoulder, which needs further assessment, plus Caelan Doris's absence through injury, open a door. Gleeson has started the season strongly, with a powerful showing in Munster's win over Racing 92 on Saturday. Connacht's Sean Jansen remains a rival for the spot."
