          "body": "Stuart Hogg's MBE was removed in March after his domestic abuse conviction, and the Cabinet Office's official register lists him among 15 people stripped of honours in 2026. Hogg won 100 caps for Scotland, toured three times with the British and Irish Lions and was twice named Six Nations Player of the Championship. He pleaded guilty to a domestic abuse charge involving his estranged wife and received a one-year community payback order in January 2025."
