          "body": "Tomos Williams is the first name on Wales's scrum-half list, and that is becoming a planning question. He has started every Test he has been available for since Steve Tandy took over in the summer of 2025, and played 378 minutes of the 2026 Six Nations. Behind him, Kieran Hardy faces a lengthy lay-off after a knee injury against Dragons, which could open the door for Reuben Morgan-Williams. Tandy names his squad today."
